# Shell scripts and git hooks must check out with LF on every platform, including Git for
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true. A CRLF byte in a shebang is the difference between a hook
# that runs and one that reports "bad interpreter".
#
# Deliberately not `* text=auto eol=lf`: that renormalizes the entire tree on next checkout,
# which is a far larger change than the one being made here.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
